## H1 — Temporary validation hosting

This is intentionally small and disposable.

Technical work:

Change the server to use:

server.listen(Number(process.env.PORT ?? 3000), "0.0.0.0");

Add /health.
Add a production start command.
Commit a dependency lockfile.
Deploy to a managed Node/container host.
Enable HTTPS.
Restrict access to invited testers.
Add robots.txt and X-Robots-Tag: noindex.
Disable request-body and profile logging.
Add security headers and body-size limits.
Record exact code/data version.
Set a shutdown date.

Restrictions:

No names, phone numbers or certificates.
Prefer synthetic marks during the first test.
No LLM keys required.
No public indexing.
No permanent database.
Stop the endpoint after observation.

## H2 — Hardened pilot hosting

After UI, RAG and optional LLM integration:

Rate limiting.
Secret management.
Structured privacy-safe monitoring.
Error correlation without student data.
Deployment rollback.
Versioned data snapshot.
Access revocation.
Backup/shutdown procedure.
LLM request and cost controls if enabled.
Mobile and security verification.

## Revised execution order

E0
 → M3-A Chat UI
 → M3-B Personal guidance
 → H1 Temporary private hosting
 → V1 First remote student validation
 → M4 Controlled RAG
 → LLM-G Optional LLM
